  "source": "marked",
  "situation": "the petition for daily bread said in the words that refuse bread. Christ to the tempter: *man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God.* This is the second time in two leaves that the fourth petition is made out of a text against bread — set II built it from Job's self-curse of thistles for wheat. The petition is never simply asked."
 },
