  "page": 350,
  "line": 23,
  "situation": "The doxology is here, and the Latin Bible does not have it. *Quia Tuum est regnum, potentia et gloria* is absent from the Vulgate at Matt. vi. 13 and from the Roman rite, which keeps it apart from the prayer; it stands in the Greek text and in the Greek liturgies. On a Latin page, its presence is a mark of which prayer-book was actually to hand.",
