   66
  ],
  "printed": "Matt. xxvi. 65, 66",
  "page": 311,
  "line": 20,
  "situation": "The 1853 editor's supplied references have an error rate of their own, and this is the second instance on two pages. `[*Vers.* 55, 56.]` under *blasphemiæ condemnari* points at *are ye come out as against a thief* and *all the disciples forsook him*; the condemnation for blasphemy is Matt. xxvi. 65, 66. One page back, his `[*Mar.* xiii. 33.]` should be xiv. 33. Both are single-digit slips, both inside his square brackets, and neither is Andrewes'. This bears on how much weight a bracketed reference can carry anywhere in the volume: the three kinds of attribution are not of equal reliability either, and the editor's is the one now shown to be fallible twice in two leaves. Kept as printed.",
  "source": "identified",
  "band": "R",
  "plateFigure": true
 },
